        <mxCell id="RG5WYI_STCJGxj8KXgSP-72" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;textShadow=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;labelBackgroundColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;CentOS&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;The &lt;b&gt;CentOS Project&lt;/b&gt; releases the &lt;b&gt;CentOS&lt;/b&gt; Linux distribution. It will be one of the most popular free and open-source community-supported computing platform, functionally compatible with its upstream source RHEL.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;CentOS will overtake the Debian distribution to become the most popular distribution for Linux servers. A few years later it will join the Red Hat corporation as an independent project.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;It will be discontinued a few decades later &lt;br&gt;in favor of its successor, &lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;CentOS Stream&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
