        <mxCell id="RG5WYI_STCJGxj8KXgSP-92" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;textShadow=0;align=left;verticalAlign=top;labelBackgroundColor=none;" value="&lt;h3 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Yocto&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;The &lt;b&gt;Linux Foundation&lt;/b&gt; announces &lt;b&gt;Yocto&lt;/b&gt;, a collaborative open-source project whose goal is to &lt;i&gt;produce tools and processes&lt;/i&gt; that enable the creation of &lt;i&gt;Linux distributions&lt;/i&gt; for &lt;i&gt;embedded&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;IoT software&lt;/i&gt; that are independent of the host architecture, supports customization and results in repeatable output.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Yocto will later become one of the biggest open-source projects to exist.&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
